[size=5][b]Alan Wake collectibles tracker[/b][/size]
[b]For the original Alan Wake (2010), NOT Alan Wake Remastered.[/b] Tested only with the Steam version, on Windows and on Linux (Steam Deck).

The statistics screen only gives game-wide totals. This mod shows [b]what you still have to find in each episode and chapter[/b].

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]In-game overlay[/b]: found / total for your current chapter and its episode, updated as you pick things up.
[*][b]Missing list[/b] (F10): which items are left in your current chapter, numbered within the chapter. Page titles (F1) and item details (F2: cutout names, where some chests and signs are) are optional.
[*][b]Menu counts[/b]: each episode and chapter shows what is left, per type.
[*]Manuscript pages, coffee thermoses, can pyramids, chests, radio shows, TV shows, signs, and both special episodes (alarm clocks, cardboard cutouts, video games).
[*]Nightmare-only manuscript pages counted separately.
[*]Hotkeys (F8 overlay, F9 menu counts, F10 missing list, F1 page titles, F2 item details) and a settings file for position, keys and text size.
[*]No game file is replaced, and nothing is sent anywhere.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]In Steam, right-click Alan Wake, then Manage, then Browse local files.
[*]If there is already a d3d9.dll there (from another mod, such as ReShade), rename it to [b]d3d9_next.dll[/b]. This mod will load it.
[*]Copy [b]d3d9.dll[/b] from the archive into that folder, next to AlanWake.exe.
[*]Start the game as usual.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstallation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Delete d3d9.dll, alanwake_collectibles.ini and alanwake_collectibles.log from the game folder.
[*]If you renamed another mod's file to d3d9_next.dll, rename it back to d3d9.dll.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]
The first time you start the game with the mod, it creates [b]alanwake_collectibles.ini[/b] in the game folder, next to AlanWake.exe. Open it with any text editor. Edits apply the next time you start the game. Delete the file to restore the defaults.

[b]Options section[/b] (1 = on, 0 = off)
[list]
[*][b]overlay[/b] (default 1): show the overlay.
[*][b]menu_counts[/b] (default 1): show counts in the episode and chapter menus.
[*][b]menu_detail[/b] (default 1): menu lists show each type left to find; 0 shows totals only.
[*][b]menu_small_text[/b] (default 1): counts in menu lists are smaller than the names; 0 uses the normal size.
[*][b]menu_hooks[/b] (default 1): 0 leaves the game's menus completely untouched (no menu counts).
[*][b]overlay_expanded[/b] (default 0): list what is missing under the counts.
[*][b]page_titles[/b] (default 0): page titles instead of page numbers in that list.
[*][b]item_details[/b] (default 0): cutout names, and where some chests and signs are, in that list.
[/list]

[b]Keys section[/b] (F1 to F24, or none)
[list]
[*][b]overlay[/b] (default F8), [b]menu_counts[/b] (F9), [b]overlay_expanded[/b] (F10), [b]page_titles[/b] (F1) and [b]item_details[/b] (F2).
[*][b]menu_detail[/b], [b]menu_small_text[/b] and [b]menu_hooks[/b] (default none) can be given a key too.
[*]A key switches the option of the same name and saves your choice. It acts at once, except for menu_small_text and menu_hooks, which apply at the next start.
[*]F5 is the game's default manuscript key, so avoid it.
[/list]

[b]Position section[/b] (where the overlay sits)
[list]
[*][b]corner[/b] (default bottom-left): or top-left, top-right, bottom-right.
[*][b]margin_x[/b] (default 1): distance from the side, in % of the screen width (0 to 90).
[*][b]margin_y[/b] (default 9): distance from the top or bottom, in % of the screen height (0 to 90).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]The original Alan Wake (2010) only.[/b] Not for Alan Wake Remastered.
[*]Tested only with the Steam version, on Windows and on Linux (Steam Deck).
[*]GOG and Epic versions are not supported.
[*]Menu counts need the Steam executable dated 2020-05-15; on others they switch off by themselves.
[*]The mod's text is in English, whatever the game's language.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]"Current chapter" is the chapter of your last checkpoint.
[*][b]Warning:[/b] the numbering in the missing list was extracted from the game data and may not be the order in which you find the items in game. The names shown for some chests and signs also come from the game's code and may not match what you see in game.
[*]An antivirus may flag the DLL, as it may any DLL that hooks into a game.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Licence[/b][/size]
MIT: you may share and adapt this mod, keeping the copyright and licence notice.

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]
[b]0.8.0[/b] List of missing items in the current chapter (F10), with optional page titles (F1) and item details (F2). Fixed: a possible crash when another program or Windows hooks Direct3D on top of the mod; game or Steam folders with non-Latin names.
[b]0.7.1[/b] First public release.
